    "kit": {
      "info": {
        "contact": {
          "name": "Open Data Plattform öV Schweiz",
          "url": "https://www.opentransportdata.swiss"
        },
        "description": "This API provides departure, delay, and cancellation data from the Swiss Federal Railways (SBB) for the previous day. It compares scheduled (soll) vs. actual (ist) operations.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "SBB Open Data API Server",
            "url": "https://data.sbb.ch/api/explore/v2.1"
          }
        ],
        "termsOfService": "https://data.sbb.ch",
        "title": "Swiss Federal Railways (SBB)",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Browse Swiss Federal Railways (SBB) open datasets — infrastructure, timetables, and previous-day soll/ist performance",
        "homepage": "https://data.sbb.ch/",
        "docs_url": "https://data.sbb.ch/api/explore/v2.1/console",
        "license_short": "Open data — non-commercial and commercial use allowed, attribution required (see SBB licence page).",
        "license_md": "- Datasets are published by SBB under terms summarised as `NonCommercialAllowed-CommercialAllowed-ReferenceRequired`.\n- Attribution to SBB / Schweizerische Bundesbahnen is required when reusing the data.\n- Some datasets ultimately originate from [opentransportdata.swiss](https://opentransportdata.swiss/) and may carry additional terms.\n- Full licence text: <https://data.sbb.ch/page/licence>.",
        "about_md": "[Swiss Federal Railways (SBB / Schweizerische Bundesbahnen)](https://www.sbb.ch/) publishes a wide-ranging open data portal at [data.sbb.ch](https://data.sbb.ch/). The portal is powered by [OpenDataSoft](https://www.opendatasoft.com/) and exposes a standard Explore v2.1 REST API for searching, filtering and exporting the underlying datasets.\n\nFor this SDK the focus is the previous-day operational data — the actual vs. scheduled (`ist` vs. `soll`) record of departures, arrivals, delays and cancellations across the SBB network. Each row typically carries the scheduled and effective times for a stop, the operator, line and a status flag for cancellations, so it can be joined back to other timetable or station datasets.\n\nWhat you can do via the API:\n\n- Query individual records of a dataset with filters, sorts and aggregations using the OpenDataSoft Query Language (ODSQL).\n- Export full result sets as JSON, CSV, GeoJSON, Parquet or Excel.\n- Browse the dataset catalog and discover other SBB open datasets (infrastructure, station equipment, ridership, etc.).\n\nOperational notes: the v2.1 API does not require authentication for public datasets, though anonymous use is rate-limited by the OpenDataSoft platform. The previous-day dataset is refreshed daily and is not a real-time feed; for live train positions use other SBB/opentransportdata.swiss services.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "export": "Bulk export of a dataset's records in a chosen format (JSON, CSV, GeoJSON, Parquet, Excel), via `/catalog/datasets/{dataset_id}/exports/{format}`.",
          "record": "An individual row of a dataset — for the SBB previous-day feed, one scheduled stop with its soll/ist times and cancellation flag — retrieved via `/catalog/datasets/{dataset_id}/records`."
        },
        "auth": false
      },
